ion-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-269370"] ["question-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)={y}^{T}Ax$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 & 14 & -28 \\\\ 14 & 14 & -28\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1e3a6cde-fe2e-5328-94cb-e127be547cc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e3a6cde-fe2e-5328-94cb-e127be547cc6"] ["answer-0f99e9f1-58c4-5851-9600-8204fd87374e" :answer/id #uuid "0f99e9f1-58c4-5851-9600-8204fd87374e"] ["answer-0f99e9f1-58c4-5851-9600-8204fd87374e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0f99e9f1-58c4-5851-9600-8204fd87374e" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-902a2d7e-4845-5624-8b64-c075f831f4cb" :answer/id #uuid "902a2d7e-4845-5624-8b64-c075f831f4cb"] ["answer-902a2d7e-4845-5624-8b64-c075f831f4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-902a2d7e-4845-56