ae" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1e3a6cde-fe2e-5328-94cb-e127be547cc6"] [17592186204080 :knowledge-point/questions "question-34c44cc9-bf3e-5025-8ef7-d8fd637a6eae"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/id #uuid "b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-269387"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)={y}^{T}Ax$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7"] ["answer-d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d" :answer/id #uuid "d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d"] ["answer-d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d" :answer/id #uuid "f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d"] ["answer-f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6" :answer/id #uuid "5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6"] ["answer-5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b" :answer/id #uuid "ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b"] ["answer-ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c" :answer/id #uuid "fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c"] ["answer-fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/correct "answer-ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b"] ["answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c"] ["question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7"] [17592186204080 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba"] ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/id #uuid "078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313"] ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/math-academy-id "q-269466"] ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$760$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-40$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=2{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=4{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i}.\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $4$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x,$ so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=4y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =4y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4([\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}76 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}760 & 760 \\\\ -40 & -40\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-86a09f03-3f8a-5c3f-9183-dbfb9af6dd2a" :answer-field/id #uuid "86a09f03-3f8a-5c3f-9183-dbfb9af6dd2a"] ["answer-b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b" :answer/id #uuid "b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b"] ["answer-b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b" :answer/value "